# SYNOPSIS

```text
protocol todhchai.radharc.Layout version 10
call name() -> String
call arrange(area: Area, windows: [UInt32], focused: UInt32, params: String)
  -> [Area]
call act(verb: String, windows: [UInt32], focused: UInt32, params: String)
  throws(WindowError) -> LayoutChange
```

# DESCRIPTION

A layout for `tile` workspaces, called by Radharc. It holds no
state: each call carries the workspace's windows in their order, the
one focused and the parameters, which Radharc keeps.

Protocol `todhchai.radharc.Layout`, version 10, of library `RadharcIPC`, its messages in the one wire format (wire(6)).

| Method | Kind | Since | Ordinal |
| `name` | call | 1 | `0x761169a793344991` |
| `arrange` | call | 1 | `0xb68014dfb7c21c6` |
| `act` | call | 1 | `0x55b7d5011c561166` |

: `name`
  Its name, which workspaces choose it by.
: `arrange`
  A frame (decorations included) for each window, in `area`.
: `act`
  A verb: the order, focus and parameters after it; `invalid` if the
  layout doesn't know it.

